   "testo": "Campobasso offers a compact historic centre, with uphill streets, stone buildings and glimpses that lead to Monforte Castle, one of its main landmarks. The Samnite Museum preserves finds that help you learn about the ancient peoples of the area and their relationship with Rome. Churches such as San Bartolomeo bear witness to the long continuity of local religious and artistic life. The city also maintains a craft tradition, linked among other things to metalworking, and a cuisine that makes the most of produce from the interior. Its small scale makes it possible to read the link between the hilly landscape and urban development.",
